Z||000000||dogtired||04-28-2000||03:50 AM||||Ok have seen this discussed several places and several ways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Has anyone currently on the list taken out a getrag 5speed and put in a Isuzu. ?<BR>I realize this is not the way most want to go   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> but I have a getrag with syncros going out and I have a good Isuzu sitting here.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>So if I trade them will I have to change the shifter cables or anything else???<BR>What will I run into and  what will be the problems???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Just trying to make do with what I have! <BR>Thanks, Where is Monkeyman??<BR><p>[This message has been edited by dogtired (edited 04-28-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||fiero56||04-28-2000||01:43 PM||||Hey Dog!!! I've been wondering when we would hear from you again.<BR>When do you plan to pull that Getrag? Any plans for it after you pull it? How far gone are the syncros, and which ones? I'm a little interested in it if you don't want/need it.<P>Monkeys out back mowing the lawn so I can stay here and type. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I think he's been working a lot lately.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||04-28-2000||07:10 PM||||The Getrag cables are different and you would need to install the Isuzu cables with the Isuzu tranny. If you look at the Getrag shift points you will notice the smaller cable actually moves it's lever up and down while the Isuzu has a lever and a pivot piont to do this. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||04-28-2000||07:43 PM||||Dogtired!<P>You will also need the throwout bearing and a slave cylinder for the Isuzu.<P><BR>BTW, I am typing this @ the hotel in Huntsville, AL after the first day @ Ed's Swap Meet!<P>I hope there are more people bringing stuff tomorrow as there were only "vendors" there selling today.  <P>You need anything that I can bring back to Wichita for you?<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||04-29-2000||04:22 PM||||Dogtired, you will need the clutch parts for the Isuzu. So in other words when you go to order your parts don't even mention the motor... just say you need the clutch for an Isuzu transaxle. I been down this road before and ended up dropping the cradle again to take out the wrong clutch and install an Isuzu setup.<P>Just my $2.02||||reg||1
